+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** Players lose runs to packet drops they cannot see — the sim knows every drop reason (enums + events exist) but the game shows no drop diagnosis. The 5.7 D-key debug overlay existed but NEVER worked in practice: its wiring is PP_DEBUG-gated end to end and no dev-run path ever builds with the define, so the user's game builds carried zero overlay code (root cause: dead launch path, not a broken key binding — the chain poll→map→exec→effect→draw is complete in code). A dev-mode NOC-style dashboard is wanted: one WORKING debug surface.
+
+**Approach:** A PP_DEBUG-gated debug surface (D key — the established 5.7 debug-key slot, user-ruled final) that is the ONE overlay: the 5.7 D overlay's unique content is ABSORBED (global line, per-class SLA table, per-pipe select readout, map heat tints, event tail) into the NOC panel (drop counters + per-class breakdown with rolling rates, crisis root-cause + rejection readouts, per-pipe queue bars vs the E9 bound, pool utilization vs the E22 cap, over-100% pipe util, scrollable last-drop alarm feed). The dead D key binding is removed. All data read-only from events/stats/topology; zero sim impact. A real dev-run path (`tools/run-dev.sh`) + a mechanical end-to-end key-toggle proof ship with it (rulings 2026-08-22: Q1-Q4 + the D-lesson amendment + the readability amendment: the dashboard must be easy to read — tabular numerals, hierarchy, dark plate, canon threshold colors, zebra drop log, >=14px text, KYLE-verified).
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- ZERO determinism impact: read-only over the sim — no state mutation, no new randomness, no timing changes. T1/T2/replay byte-identical with the overlay ON. No sim-side changes; only view-layer reads + app-owned accumulator state.
+- Dev-gated: all drawing under `when #config(PP_DEBUG, false)` (release + every harness build compile it out); D key polled only in PP_DEBUG builds; overlay OFF by default; normal runs byte-identical. The dev launch is FIRST-CLASS: `tools/run-dev.sh` builds+runs with the define (the D root cause was the missing launch path — the surface must be reachable).
+- ONE working debug surface, ONE key: D is THE debug overlay (the 5.7 slot, user-ruled final — one key, one panel, zero dead code). The 5.7 D overlay is absorbed — its unique content (heat tints, SLA/latency/loss class columns, per-pipe select readout, all-tag event tail, score/meter line) folds into the merged panel; `app/render/debug_overlay.odin` and the D key binding are removed. No second surface, no forked copies (the #82 N15 anti-pattern).
+- Taxonomy maps 1:1 to code enums: drop counters = `Drop_Reason.Queue_Overflow` (E9) + `Drop_Reason.Pool_Exhaustion` (E22); crisis root causes from `Root_Cause_Kind` via `EVENT_TAG_CRISIS_TRIGGERED`; rejections labeled "rejected, not dropped" (`Edit_Error`, e.g. Router_Ports_Full). Any drop path not classified = a finding, not a guess.
+- SHARE, never fork: reuse `draw_text_c` / `draw_panel_card`; the NOC feed is the one shared accumulator/ring (the visibility layer's `feed_drop_sites`/`drop_marks`/`drop_reasons` stay untouched); no duplicate event scan.
+- END-TO-END proof the D toggle works in a REAL game run (the D lesson): a PP_DEBUG auto-drive mode injects the D key's Device_Event through the REAL input pipeline and captures the panel ON and OFF (mechanical screenshots), plus an input-layer @(test) pinning Key_Press{D} → Toggle_Overlay → effect.
+- READABILITY (user ruling 2026-08-22, final): tabular figures — all live numbers right-aligned in FIXED columns, zero width-jitter as counters tick (the HUD font's digits are tabular: Open Sans equal advances — verified); hierarchy — 10px uppercase labels, >=14px body (the 5.8 QoS-panel legibility convention), 22px headline numerals, the DROPS counters are the headline row; a DARK semi-opaque backing plate so text reads over any map state; threshold colors from game canon — balance.json `warnings.pipe_amber_pct` (70) / `pipe_red_pct` (90) for the utilization + queue bars AND the heat tints (the 5.7 custom 50/70/90 ladder is superseded); drop log zebra-striped with fixed columns; readable at the 1280x720 window.
+- Follow view-layer conventions: `draw_text_c` ASCII only, explicit params on draw procs (harness-renderable), no map iteration, no per-frame allocations (fixed arrays only).
+
+**Ask First:** nothing anticipated — the rulings cover the open decisions.
+
+**Never:** no changes to core/ sim files (enums, flow, stats, crisis), no event-buffer mutation/draining, no golden re-bless, no edits to `data/*.json`, no aesthetic ceremony (dev tool — keep the engine's current style), no vision verdicts. The visibility layer (`drop_marks`/`drop_reasons`/`feed_drop_sites`) and the harness golden drivers are untouched.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| D key in a real PP_DEBUG run | real windowed app, key press | panel appears; second press hides it; captures prove both states | e2e auto-drive + input-layer test pin the chain |
+| Unknown drop reason byte | `Packet_Dropped` reason ∉ {Queue_Overflow, Pool_Exhaustion} | "other/unclassified" bucket + raw reason in log row | never mislabeled as E9/E22 |
+| Class id beyond table | class ≥ roster (catalog data-driven) | row skipped without a name; count still lands | bounded index guard |
+| >60-tick scan gap | ticks pass with no drops between feeds | tick-keyed ring rolls; rates = last 60 ticks only | deterministic at any frame/tick interleave |
+| Drop burst > 256 | >256 drops in window | ring wraps: oldest evicted, newest-first, capped 256 | fixed array — no allocation |
+| Rejection outside sim stream | `input.last_reject` transitions (app-only) | counter per new reject_tick; harness shows 0 (honest) | optional feed input |
+| Both overlays on | n/a — ONE surface | D is the only toggle; no overlap state exists | removed by design |
