+## Design Notes
+
+- **Events, not drop_sites:** the per-tick scratch is valid only right after `pp.step`; `Packet_Dropped`/`CRISIS_TRIGGERED` events ARE the serialized record. App and harness reach identical feed states from the same stream (@(test) pins incremental==one-shot).
+- **Tick-keyed rings:** rate rings zero-fill skipped slots on batch spans (`slot = tick % 60`; clear the 60 slots for [ring_tick+1, ring_tick+60]) — frame/tick interleave cannot corrupt rates; a jump ≥60 clears all.
+- **Ungated feed, gated draws:** feed + scan are pure fixed-array code (no raylib) so gate-2's `odin test app/render` runs the tests — no CI changes. Release carries an inert ~9 KB accumulator; every draw/input path stays under `when #config(PP_DEBUG, false)`.
+- **Log lane/endpoints:** the drop event carries bundle only. At draw, resolve read-only: bundle → live pipes (`bundles.pipe_bundle`, slot order) → endpoint ids; lane = `qos_lane_of(pipe, dropped_class)` on the bundle's first live pipe. E22 rows show "map-wide". Stale slots (renumbered by a rebuild) render "gone" rather than misanchoring.
+- **Rejections:** fed app-side from `last_reject`/`reject_tick` transitions, per-kind into a fixed [32]u32 table (Edit_Error < 32). Harness replay never rejects — overlay-check shows 0.
+- **e2e drive honesty:** the auto-drive injects the exact `Device_Event(Key_Press{.D})` the PP_DEBUG poller creates, AFTER the polls and BEFORE `dispatch_frame` — the real map→exec→effect→draw chain runs untouched; only the key SOURCE is scripted (the parity-harness doctrine).
+- **Proof chain:** AC3 = overlay-check sidecar vs blessed `.t1` (`cmp`); harness suite green = T2/replay untouched; `when` gate + OFF-by-default = release byte-identity; e2e captures + input test = the key chain in a real run; @(test) = taxonomy + purity.
+
